course: dictionary
lesson: 8746
title: One word, two meanings: servo
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word servo is one of them. In a robot lesson, a servo is a small motor that turns to an exact position and holds it, such as 90 degrees.
explain: In Australia, a servo is a petrol station, short for «service station». Rian is puzzled by a sentence from his cousins: «Let's go to the servo for a snag!» The clue is the trip: you stop for petrol, snacks and a drink on a road trip, so a servo must be a place.
explain: When a word has two meanings, look at the words around it. Ask: what would fit here, a motor or a place? Then try that meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Servo is a noun. You can have one servo or two servos.
fact: A servo, short for servomotor, is a small motor that can turn to an exact position and hold it.
fact: In Australia, servo means petrol station, short for «service station».
fact: Programmers can use a micro:bit or Arduino to turn a servo to a set angle, such as 90 degrees.
fact: The same word can mean different things in different places, so context tells you which meaning is right.
exercise: In a robot lesson, Mia programs a servo to turn to 90 degrees. What is a servo here? | A metal plate on a bridge | A robot's head that sings | A dog that fetches the ball | *A small motor that turns to an exact position and holds it
exercise: Ella is in Australia. Her friend says, «Let's stop at the servo for petrol.» Where are they going? | A bus stop | A swimming pool | A school gym | *A petrol station
exercise: «Let's go to the servo for a snag!» What is a servo in this sentence? | A type of sausage | *A petrol station | A robot | A motor
test: «The servo turned the gate arm to 90 degrees.» In this sentence, servo means? | *A small motor | A type of hat | A bus driver | A petrol station
test: An Aussie says, «I'm stopping at the servo for a drink.» Where is the speaker going? | A park | A school | *A petrol station | A bank
exam: Why is Rian confused? | Australians never use the word servo | A snag is a petrol station | He thinks his cousin is a robot | *He does not know that servo means a petrol station in Australia
